      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin in adults, which is 2,550 mg/day. The extended-release maximum is 2,000 mg/day in the US. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual 850 mg to 1,000 mg per-dose ceiling. Metformin at that level raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day total.** That could be 850 mg PO twice daily with meals, or another split.\n- **A different dose or drug.** The 1,700 may be a typo or a unit mix-up.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it. If you really need a dose above the labeled maximum, it will need to go through pharmacy or the attending. I can't enter it based on a statement of approval."
      }
     ],
